  "worked_solution": "To determine whether the sequence converges or diverges, we need to determine the limit of the sequence as $n$ approaches infinity:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{5{n}^{2}+7}{3{n}^{3}-2}.\n$$\n\nThe dominant term in the denominator is $3{n}^{3},$ so we divide the numerator and the denominator by ${n}^{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{5{n}^{2}+7}{3{n}^{3}-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{5{n}^{2}}{{n}^{3}}+\\frac{7}{{n}^{3}})}{(\\frac{3{n}^{3}}{{n}^{3}}-\\frac{2}{{n}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\frac{5}{n}+\\frac{7}{{n}^{3}}}{3-\\frac{2}{{n}^{3}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+0}{3-0} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the limit exists, the sequence converges, and its limit is $0.$",
